& [UserVision]
  + use Cantor as an agent process soon
  + one slim Cantor hosts a first LLM such as Needle or Needle 2 running SOP
  + that hosted SOP executes a contract that loads and runs another LLM
  + the slim Cantor agent is the launch pad for a larger Cantor and its LLM
  + the outer and inner Cantor negotiate a shared attention window and shared perspective during inference
  + Cantor therefore runs a Cantor that runs the full system

& [RequiredDistinctions]
  + outer Cantor process identity is distinct from outer model identity
  + inner Cantor process identity is distinct from inner model identity
  + launch authority model-loading authority inference authority and attention-negotiation authority are separate contracts
  + shared attention is an explicit negotiated evidence surface and not an implied shared hidden state
  + custody ownership resource bounds faults restart loss and completion remain explicit

& [ExistingSubstrateToAudit]
  + EVO-X2 Needle2 SOP Attention Runtime
  + shared-attention imagination runtime tool adapter CLI and MCP surface
  + supervised local service lifecycle and authenticated operator surface
  + iterative attention loop checkpoint custody discovery replay and lifecycle bridge
  + seeded compiler external-inference host and native-candidate lifecycle specifications

& [SourceBoundary]
  + this source preserves the current-thread user vision only
  + independently untracked neural-host identity-virtualization semantic-host-network and related drafts are not imported edited staged or treated as authority
  + no provider model download installation process launch second-model execution persistence remote effect FPGA or Minecraft action is authorized by preservation alone

& [Next]
  + perform a source-to-existing-substrate gap audit
  + form separate SJS contracts for outer host inner launch model identity custody and negotiated shared-attention inference before implementation
